<Project>

    <!--
      Intentionally empty, and the twin of Directory.Build.props beside it.

      MSBuild stops walking up at the first Directory.Build.targets, so this shields the tooling under
      build/ from the repository root file - which imports RefCheck into every Revit-side project.
      Without this, RefCheck's own project would import the targets that build RefCheck.

      The import at the root is already conditional on $(RevitVersion), so nothing here is load
      bearing today. It exists so that the shield is a pair rather than a habit somebody has to
      remember, which is how the props file came to be there in the first place.
    -->

</Project>
